IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `pip-nouns`
IMPORT `pip-dates`
IMPORT `pip-sch1-daily-living-table`
IMPORT `pip-sch1-mobility-table`

-- PART 2 -- PERSONAL INDEPENDENCE PAYMENT ASSESSMENT: regulations 3 to 11.
--
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. The assessment turns a finding of fact (which descriptor C
-- satisfies, on how many days) into points (Schedule 1) and the points into a level of ability.
-- Whether a descriptor is satisfied on a day is a judgment the text hands to the Secretary of
-- State ("it is likely that, if C had been assessed on that day, C would have satisfied that
-- descriptor", reg 7(2)); it enters here as an input and is never guessed.

§ `Regulation 3: daily living activities and mobility activities`

-- reg 3(1): for the purposes of section 78(4) of the Act and these Regulations, daily living
-- activities are the activities set out in column 1 of the table in Part 2 of Schedule 1.
-- out of text: Welfare Reform Act 2012 s 78(4)
-- src:38 | (1) For the purposes of section 78(4) of the Act and these Regulations, daily living activities are the activities set out in column 1 of the table in Part 2 of Schedule 1.
@ref reg 3(1) (src:38)
GIVETH A LIST OF `an activity of Schedule 1`
`reg 3(1): the daily living activities` MEANS
    LIST `daily living activity 1, preparing food`
       , `daily living activity 2, taking nutrition`
       , `daily living activity 3, managing therapy or monitoring a health condition`
       , `daily living activity 4, washing and bathing`
       , `daily living activity 5, managing toilet needs or incontinence`
       , `daily living activity 6, dressing and undressing`
       , `daily living activity 7, communicating verbally`
       , `daily living activity 8, reading and understanding signs, symbols and words`
       , `daily living activity 9, engaging with other people face to face`
       , `daily living activity 10, making budgeting decisions`

@ref reg 3(1) (src:38)
GIVEN a IS AN `an activity of Schedule 1`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 3(1): this is a daily living activity` a MEANS
    elem a (`reg 3(1): the daily living activities`)

-- reg 3(2): for the purposes of section 79(4) of the Act and these Regulations, mobility
-- activities are the activities set out in column 1 of the table in Part 3 of Schedule 1.
-- out of text: Welfare Reform Act 2012 s 79(4)
-- src:39 | (2) For the purposes of section 79(4) of the Act and these Regulations, mobility activities are the activities set out in column 1 of the table in Part 3 of Schedule 1.
@ref reg 3(2) (src:39)
GIVETH A LIST OF `an activity of Schedule 1`
`reg 3(2): the mobility activities` MEANS
    LIST `mobility activity 1, planning and following journeys`
       , `mobility activity 2, moving around`

@ref reg 3(2) (src:39)
GIVEN a IS AN `an activity of Schedule 1`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 3(2): this is a mobility activity` a MEANS
    elem a (`reg 3(2): the mobility activities`)

§ `Regulation 4: assessment of ability to carry out activities`

-- reg 4(1): whether C has limited or severely limited ability to carry out daily living or mobility
-- activities, as a result of C's physical or mental condition, is determined on the basis of an
-- assessment (the level that regs 5(3) and 6(3) find). If the limitation is not a result of C's
-- physical or mental condition, reg 4(1) gives C neither level.
-- out of text: Welfare Reform Act 2012 ss 77(2), 78, 79
-- src:41 | (1) For the purposes of section 77(2) and section 78 or 79, as the case may be, of the Act, whether C has limited or severely limited ability to carry out daily living or mobility activities, as a result of C's physical or mental condition, is to be determined on the basis of an assessment.
@ref reg 4(1) (src:41)
GIVEN `the level of ability found on the assessment` IS A `a level of ability to carry out activities`
      `the limitation is a result of C's physical or mental condition` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `a level of ability to carry out activities`
`reg 4(1): C's level of ability, on the basis of an assessment` MEANS
    IF `the limitation is a result of C's physical or mental condition`
    THEN `the level of ability found on the assessment`
    ELSE `neither limited ability nor severely limited ability`

-- reg 4(2): C's ability to carry out an activity is assessed (a) on the basis of C's ability whilst
-- wearing or using any aid or appliance which C normally wears or uses; or (b) as if C were wearing or
-- using any aid or appliance which C could reasonably be expected to wear or use. The two limbs
-- reach different aids (one C actually uses, one C could reasonably be expected to use), so an aid
-- is taken into account if either limb reaches it (fork F-4).
-- src:42 | (2) C's ability to carry out an activity is to be assessed –
-- src:43 | (a) on the basis of C's ability whilst wearing or using any aid or appliance which C normally wears or uses; or
-- src:44 | (b) as if C were wearing or using any aid or appliance which C could reasonably be expected to wear or use.
@ref reg 4(2) (src:42-44)
GIVEN `C normally wears or uses the aid or appliance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `C could reasonably be expected to wear or use the aid or appliance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 4(2): C's ability is assessed as if C were wearing or using the aid or appliance` MEANS
       `C normally wears or uses the aid or appliance`
    OR `C could reasonably be expected to wear or use the aid or appliance`

-- reg 4(4)(a): "safely" means in a manner unlikely to cause harm to C or to another person, either
-- during or after completion of the activity.
-- src:52 | (a) “safely” means in a manner unlikely to cause harm to C or to another person, either during or after completion of the activity;
@ref reg 4(4)(a) (src:52)
GIVEN `harm to C is likely during or after completion of the activity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `harm to another person is likely during or after completion of the activity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 4(4)(a): the activity is done safely` MEANS
        (NOT `harm to C is likely during or after completion of the activity`)
    AND (NOT `harm to another person is likely during or after completion of the activity`)

-- reg 4(4)(b): "repeatedly" means as often as the activity being assessed is reasonably required to be completed.
-- src:53 | (b) “repeatedly” means as often as the activity being assessed is reasonably required to be completed; and
@ref reg 4(4)(b) (src:53)
GIVEN `the number of times C can complete the activity` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of times the activity is reasonably required to be completed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 4(4)(b): the activity is done repeatedly` MEANS
    `the number of times C can complete the activity`
        AT LEAST `the number of times the activity is reasonably required to be completed`

-- reg 4(4)(c): "reasonable time period" means no more than twice as long as the maximum period that a
-- person without a physical or mental condition which limits that person's ability to carry out the
-- activity in question would normally take to complete that activity.
-- src:54 | (c) “reasonable time period” means no more than twice as long as the maximum period that a person without a physical or mental condition which limits that person’s ability to carry out the activity in question would normally take to complete that activity.
@ref reg 4(4)(c) (src:54)
GIVEN `the time C takes to complete the activity` IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum time a person without a limiting condition would normally take` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 4(4)(c): the activity is done within a reasonable time period` MEANS
    `the time C takes to complete the activity`
        AT MOST (2 TIMES `the maximum time a person without a limiting condition would normally take`)

-- reg 4(2A): where C's ability to carry out an activity is assessed, C is to be assessed as satisfying a
-- descriptor only if C can do so (a) safely; (b) to an acceptable standard; (c) repeatedly; and (d)
-- within a reasonable time period. "Only if" makes the four limbs necessary conditions, not sufficient
-- ones: this rule says whether C may be assessed as satisfying a descriptor that turns on doing the
-- activity, not that the descriptor is satisfied.
-- src:45 | (2A) Where C’s ability to carry out an activity is assessed, C is to be assessed as satisfying a descriptor only if C can do so—
-- src:46 | (a) safely;
-- src:47 | (b) to an acceptable standard;
-- src:48 | (c) repeatedly; and
-- src:49 | (d) within a reasonable time period.
@ref reg 4(2A) (src:45-49)
GIVEN `C can do the activity safely` IS A BOOLEAN
      `C can do the activity to an acceptable standard` IS A BOOLEAN
      `C can do the activity repeatedly` IS A BOOLEAN
      `C can do the activity within a reasonable time period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 4(2A): C may be assessed as satisfying a descriptor that turns on doing the activity` MEANS
        `C can do the activity safely`
    AND `C can do the activity to an acceptable standard`
    AND `C can do the activity repeatedly`
    AND `C can do the activity within a reasonable time period`

-- reg 4(2A) read with reg 4(4): the four limbs worked out from the facts that reg 4(4) names.
@ref reg 4(2A), reg 4(4) (src:45-49)
GIVEN `harm to C is likely during or after completion of the activity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `harm to another person is likely during or after completion of the activity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `C can do the activity to an acceptable standard` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of times C can complete the activity` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of times the activity is reasonably required to be completed` IS A NUMBER
      `the time C takes to complete the activity` IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum time a person without a limiting condition would normally take` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 4(2A) and (4): C may be assessed as satisfying a descriptor, from the facts` MEANS
    `reg 4(2A): C may be assessed as satisfying a descriptor that turns on doing the activity`
        `the activity is done safely`
        `C can do the activity to an acceptable standard`
        `the activity is done repeatedly`
        `the activity is done within a reasonable time period`
    WHERE
        `the activity is done safely` MEANS
            `reg 4(4)(a): the activity is done safely`
                `harm to C is likely during or after completion of the activity`
                `harm to another person is likely during or after completion of the activity`
        `the activity is done repeatedly` MEANS
            `reg 4(4)(b): the activity is done repeatedly`
                `the number of times C can complete the activity`
                `the number of times the activity is reasonably required to be completed`
        `the activity is done within a reasonable time period` MEANS
            `reg 4(4)(c): the activity is done within a reasonable time period`
                `the time C takes to complete the activity`
                `the maximum time a person without a limiting condition would normally take`

-- reg 4(3): where C has been assessed as having severely limited ability to carry out activities, C is
-- not to be treated as also having limited ability in relation to the same activities. So a score that
-- reaches both thresholds of regulation 5(3) or 6(3) gives severely limited ability alone.
-- src:50 | (3) Where C has been assessed as having severely limited ability to carry out activities, C is not to be treated as also having limited ability in relation to the same activities.
@ref reg 4(3) (src:50)
GIVEN `C has been assessed as having limited ability` IS A BOOLEAN
      `C has been assessed as having severely limited ability` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `a level of ability to carry out activities`
`reg 4(3): the level of ability C is treated as having` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `C has been assessed as having severely limited ability` THEN `severely limited ability`
        IF `C has been assessed as having limited ability` THEN `limited ability`
        OTHERWISE `neither limited ability nor severely limited ability`

§ `Regulations 5 and 6: scoring`

-- reg 5(1) and (2): the score C obtains in relation to daily living activities is the sum of the points
-- awarded for each activity in column 1 of the daily living activities table; the points for an
-- activity are the number in column 3 against whichever descriptor applies to C under regulation 7.
-- The descriptor that applies to C for each activity is the input; where regulation 7 selects
-- none for an activity (its constructor "no descriptor ... applies"), the text does not say what points
-- follow, so the score is not covered (NOTHING), and that is asserted (fork F-7).
DECLARE `the descriptors that apply to C in the daily living activities` HAS
    `for preparing food` IS A `a descriptor of daily living activity 1`
    `for taking nutrition` IS A `a descriptor of daily living activity 2`
    `for managing therapy or monitoring a health condition` IS A `a descriptor of daily living activity 3`
    `for washing and bathing` IS A `a descriptor of daily living activity 4`
    `for managing toilet needs or incontinence` IS A `a descriptor of daily living activity 5`
    `for dressing and undressing` IS A `a descriptor of daily living activity 6`
    `for communicating verbally` IS A `a descriptor of daily living activity 7`
    `for reading and understanding signs, symbols and words` IS A `a descriptor of daily living activity 8`
    `for engaging with other people face to face` IS A `a descriptor of daily living activity 9`
    `for making budgeting decisions` IS A `a descriptor of daily living activity 10`

-- The points of a descriptor are the points in its row; where a descriptor has no row the points are not covered.
GIVEN r IS A MAYBE `a row of Schedule 1`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 5(2) and reg 6(2): the points in the row against the descriptor` r MEANS
    CONSIDER r
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST x THEN JUST (x's `its points`)

-- The sum of the points of a list of descriptors: not covered if any of them is.
GIVEN points IS A LIST OF (MAYBE NUMBER)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 5(1) and reg 6(1): the points added together` points MEANS
    IF all (GIVEN p YIELD isJust p) points
    THEN JUST (sum (mapMaybe (GIVEN p YIELD p) points))
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:56 | (1) The score C obtains in relation to daily living activities is determined by adding together the number of points (if any) awarded for each activity listed in column 1 of the table in Part 2 of Schedule 1 (“the daily living activities table”).
-- src:57 | (2) For the purpose of paragraph (1), the number of points awarded to C for each activity listed in column 1 of the daily living activities table is the number shown in column 3 of the table against whichever of the descriptors set out in column 2 of the table for the activity applies to C under regulation 7.
@ref reg 5(1), reg 5(2) (src:56-57)
GIVEN d IS A `the descriptors that apply to C in the daily living activities`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 5(1): the score C obtains in daily living activities` d MEANS
    `reg 5(1) and reg 6(1): the points added together`
        (LIST `reg 5(2) and reg 6(2): the points in the row against the descriptor` (`the row of a descriptor of daily living activity 1` (d's `for preparing food`))
            , `reg 5(2) and reg 6(2): the points in the row against the descriptor` (`the row of a descriptor of daily living activity 2` (d's `for taking nutrition`))
            , `reg 5(2) and reg 6(2): the points in the row against the descriptor` (`the row of a descriptor of daily living activity 3` (d's `for managing therapy or monitoring a health condition`))
            , `reg 5(2) and reg 6(2): the points in the row against the descriptor` (`the row of a descriptor of daily living activity 4` (d's `for washing and bathing`))
            , `reg 5(2) and reg 6(2): the points in the row against the descriptor` (`the row of a descriptor of daily living activity 5` (d's `for managing toilet needs or incontinence`))
            , `reg 5(2) and reg 6(2): the points in the row against the descriptor` (`the row of a descriptor of daily living activity 6` (d's `for dressing and undressing`))
            , `reg 5(2) and reg 6(2): the points in the row against the descriptor` (`the row of a descriptor of daily living activity 7` (d's `for communicating verbally`))
            , `reg 5(2) and reg 6(2): the points in the row against the descriptor` (`the row of a descriptor of daily living activity 8` (d's `for reading and understanding signs, symbols and words`))
            , `reg 5(2) and reg 6(2): the points in the row against the descriptor` (`the row of a descriptor of daily living activity 9` (d's `for engaging with other people face to face`))
            , `reg 5(2) and reg 6(2): the points in the row against the descriptor` (`the row of a descriptor of daily living activity 10` (d's `for making budgeting decisions`)))

-- reg 5(3): where C has undergone an assessment, C has (a) limited ability to carry out daily living
-- activities where C obtains a score of at least 8 points; and (b) severely limited ability where C
-- obtains a score of at least 12 points. Read with reg 4(3): the higher level alone. Where C has
-- not undergone an assessment, or the score is not covered, the level is not covered (NOTHING).
-- src:58 | (3) Where C has undergone an assessment, C has —
-- src:59 | (a) limited ability to carry out daily living activities where C obtains a score of at least 8 points in relation to daily living activities; and
-- src:60 | (b) severely limited ability to carry out daily living activities where C obtains a score of at least 12 points in relation to daily living activities.
@ref reg 5(3) (src:58-60)
GIVEN `C has undergone an assessment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `C's score in relation to daily living activities` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `a level of ability to carry out activities`
`reg 5(3): C's level of ability to carry out daily living activities` MEANS
    IF NOT `C has undergone an assessment`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER `C's score in relation to daily living activities`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
         WHEN JUST score THEN
             JUST (`reg 4(3): the level of ability C is treated as having`
                       WITH `C has been assessed as having limited ability` IS score AT LEAST 8
                          , `C has been assessed as having severely limited ability` IS score AT LEAST 12)

-- reg 6(1) and (2): the same for mobility activities.
DECLARE `the descriptors that apply to C in the mobility activities` HAS
    `for planning and following journeys` IS A `a descriptor of mobility activity 1`
    `for moving around` IS A `a descriptor of mobility activity 2`

-- src:62 | (1) The score C obtains in relation to mobility activities is determined by adding together the number of points (if any) awarded for each activity listed in column 1 of the table in Part 3 of Schedule 1 (“the mobility activities table”).
-- src:63 | (2) For the purpose of paragraph (1), the number of points awarded to C for each activity listed in column 1 of the mobility activities table is the number shown in column 3 of the table against whichever of the descriptors set out in column 2 of the table for the activity applies to C under regulation 7.
@ref reg 6(1), reg 6(2) (src:62-63)
GIVEN d IS A `the descriptors that apply to C in the mobility activities`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 6(1): the score C obtains in mobility activities` d MEANS
    `reg 5(1) and reg 6(1): the points added together`
        (LIST `reg 5(2) and reg 6(2): the points in the row against the descriptor` (`the row of a descriptor of mobility activity 1` (d's `for planning and following journeys`))
            , `reg 5(2) and reg 6(2): the points in the row against the descriptor` (`the row of a descriptor of mobility activity 2` (d's `for moving around`)))

-- reg 6(3): the same thresholds (8 and 12) for mobility activities.
-- src:64 | (3) Where C has undergone an assessment, C has —
-- src:65 | (a) limited ability to carry out mobility activities where C obtains a score of at least 8 points in relation to mobility activities; and
-- src:66 | (b) severely limited ability to carry out mobility activities where C obtains a score of at least 12 points in relation to mobility activities.
@ref reg 6(3) (src:64-66)
GIVEN `C has undergone an assessment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `C's score in relation to mobility activities` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `a level of ability to carry out activities`
`reg 6(3): C's level of ability to carry out mobility activities` MEANS
    IF NOT `C has undergone an assessment`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER `C's score in relation to mobility activities`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
         WHEN JUST score THEN
             JUST (`reg 4(3): the level of ability C is treated as having`
                       WITH `C has been assessed as having limited ability` IS score AT LEAST 8
                          , `C has been assessed as having severely limited ability` IS score AT LEAST 12)

§ `Regulation 7: scoring, further provision`

-- reg 7(3): the "required period" is the stretch of days over which regulation 7(1) counts the days
-- on which a descriptor is satisfied. It is two windows: the 3 months ending with the prescribed date
-- and a 9-month window whose start depends on the case.
DECLARE `a required period` HAS
    `the first day of the 3 months` IS A DATE
    `the last day of the 3 months` IS A DATE
    `the first day of the 9 months` IS A DATE
    `the last day of the 9 months` IS A DATE

-- reg 7(3)(a)(i): a claim after an interval for the purpose of regulation 15 or 15A: the 3 months
-- ending with the prescribed date, together with the 9 months beginning with the date on which that
-- claim is made. (Regulation 15B is not named here: fork F-8.)
-- src:75 | (3) In paragraphs (1) and (2), “required period” means—
-- src:76 | (a) in the case where entitlement to personal independence payment falls to be determined, the period of 3 months ending with the prescribed date together with—
-- src:77 | (i) in relation to a claim after an interval for the purpose of regulation 15 or 15A, the period of 9 months beginning with the date on which that claim is made;
@ref reg 7(3)(a)(i) (src:75-77)
GIVEN `the prescribed date` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the claim is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `a required period`
`reg 7(3)(a)(i): the required period for a claim after an interval under regulation 15 or 15A` MEANS
    `a required period`
        WITH `the first day of the 3 months` IS `the first day of the months ending with` `the prescribed date` `for` 3
           , `the last day of the 3 months` IS `the prescribed date`
           , `the first day of the 9 months` IS `the date on which the claim is made`
           , `the last day of the 9 months` IS `the last day of the months beginning with` `the date on which the claim is made` `for` 9

-- reg 7(3)(a)(ii): any other claim: the 3 months ending with the prescribed date, together with the 9
-- months beginning with the day after the prescribed date.
-- src:75 | (3) In paragraphs (1) and (2), “required period” means—
-- src:76 | (a) in the case where entitlement to personal independence payment falls to be determined, the period of 3 months ending with the prescribed date together with—
-- src:78 | (ii) in relation to any other claim, the period of 9 months beginning with the day after the prescribed date.
@ref reg 7(3)(a)(ii) (src:75-76, src:78)
GIVEN `the prescribed date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `a required period`
`reg 7(3)(a)(ii): the required period for any other claim` MEANS
    `a required period`
        WITH `the first day of the 3 months` IS `the first day of the months ending with` `the prescribed date` `for` 3
           , `the last day of the 3 months` IS `the prescribed date`
           , `the first day of the 9 months` IS `the day after` `the prescribed date`
           , `the last day of the 9 months` IS `the last day of the months beginning with` (`the day after` `the prescribed date`) `for` 9

-- reg 7(3)(b)(i): where PIP has been awarded, during the 3 months following a determination of
-- entitlement under a claim for the purpose of regulation 15 or 15A: the 3 months ending with the
-- prescribed date, together with, for each day of the award, the 9 months beginning with the day after
-- that date. "That date" is read as the day of the award (fork F-9).
-- src:79 | (b) in the case where personal independence payment has been awarded to C—
-- src:80 | (i) during the period of 3 months following a determination of entitlement under a claim for the purpose of regulation 15 or 15A, the period of 3 months ending with the prescribed date together with, for each day of the award, the period of 9 months beginning with the day after that date;
@ref reg 7(3)(b)(i) (src:79-80)
GIVEN `the prescribed date` IS A DATE
      `the day of the award` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `a required period`
`reg 7(3)(b)(i): the required period for a day of an award in the 3 months after a claim for the purpose of regulation 15 or 15A` MEANS
    `a required period`
        WITH `the first day of the 3 months` IS `the first day of the months ending with` `the prescribed date` `for` 3
           , `the last day of the 3 months` IS `the prescribed date`
           , `the first day of the 9 months` IS `the day after` `the day of the award`
           , `the last day of the 9 months` IS `the last day of the months beginning with` (`the day after` `the day of the award`) `for` 9

-- reg 7(3)(b)(ii): in any other case, for each day of the award, the 3 months ending with that day
-- together with the 9 months beginning with the day after it.
-- src:79 | (b) in the case where personal independence payment has been awarded to C—
-- src:81 | (ii) in any other case, for each day of the award, the period of 3 months ending with that date together with the period of 9 months beginning with the day after that date.
@ref reg 7(3)(b)(ii) (src:79, src:81)
GIVEN `the day of the award` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `a required period`
`reg 7(3)(b)(ii): the required period for a day of an award in any other case` MEANS
    `a required period`
        WITH `the first day of the 3 months` IS `the first day of the months ending with` `the day of the award` `for` 3
           , `the last day of the 3 months` IS `the day of the award`
           , `the first day of the 9 months` IS `the day after` `the day of the award`
           , `the last day of the 9 months` IS `the last day of the months beginning with` (`the day after` `the day of the award`) `for` 9

-- The number of days of a required period: both windows, counted inclusively.
GIVEN rp IS A `a required period`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 7(3): the number of days of the required period` rp MEANS
    ((Day (rp's `the last day of the 3 months`) MINUS Day (rp's `the first day of the 3 months`)) PLUS 1)
    PLUS ((Day (rp's `the last day of the 9 months`) MINUS Day (rp's `the first day of the 9 months`)) PLUS 1)

-- reg 7(2): a descriptor is satisfied on a day in the required period if it is likely that, if C had
-- been assessed on that day, C would have satisfied that descriptor. The likelihood is a judgment
-- handed to the Secretary of State and is the input.
-- src:74 | (2) For the purposes of paragraph (1), a descriptor is satisfied on a day in the required period if it is likely that, if C had been assessed on that day, C would have satisfied that descriptor.
@ref reg 7(2) (src:74)
GIVEN `it is likely that, had C been assessed on that day, C would have satisfied the descriptor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 7(2): the descriptor is satisfied on the day` MEANS
    `it is likely that, had C been assessed on that day, C would have satisfied the descriptor`

-- reg 7(1): the descriptor which applies to C for an activity. Each candidate is a descriptor (a row
-- of Schedule 1) and the number of days of the required period on which it is satisfied.
DECLARE `a descriptor with the days on which it is satisfied` HAS
    `the descriptor` IS A `a row of Schedule 1`
    `the days of the required period on which it is satisfied` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN e IS A `a descriptor with the days on which it is satisfied`
      `the days of the required period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 7(1): this descriptor is satisfied on over 50% of the days of the required period` e `of` `the days of the required period` MEANS
    (e's `the days of the required period on which it is satisfied`) TIMES 2 GREATER THAN `the days of the required period`

-- Of a list of candidates, the one that scores the higher or highest number of points (the first, if
-- two score alike).
GIVEN es IS A LIST OF `a descriptor with the days on which it is satisfied`
GIVETH A MAYBE `a descriptor with the days on which it is satisfied`
`reg 7(1): the candidate scoring the highest number of points among` es MEANS
    CONSIDER es
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN e FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        CONSIDER `reg 7(1): the candidate scoring the highest number of points among` rest
        WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST e
        WHEN JUST r THEN
            IF (r's `the descriptor`)'s `its points` GREATER THAN (e's `the descriptor`)'s `its points`
            THEN JUST r
            ELSE JUST e

-- Of a list of candidates, the one satisfied for the greater or greatest proportion of days of the
-- required period; where they are satisfied for the same proportion, the one scoring the higher or
-- highest number of points (the first, if they also score alike).
GIVEN es IS A LIST OF `a descriptor with the days on which it is satisfied`
GIVETH A MAYBE `a descriptor with the days on which it is satisfied`
`reg 7(1)(c): the candidate satisfied on the most days, then scoring the highest number of points, among` es MEANS
    CONSIDER es
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN e FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        CONSIDER `reg 7(1)(c): the candidate satisfied on the most days, then scoring the highest number of points, among` rest
        WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST e
        WHEN JUST r THEN
            IF    (r's `the days of the required period on which it is satisfied`) GREATER THAN (e's `the days of the required period on which it is satisfied`)
               OR (    (r's `the days of the required period on which it is satisfied`) EQUALS (e's `the days of the required period on which it is satisfied`)
                   AND (r's `the descriptor`)'s `its points` GREATER THAN (e's `the descriptor`)'s `its points`)
            THEN JUST r
            ELSE JUST e

-- reg 7(1)(a): where one descriptor is satisfied on over 50% of the days of the required period, that
-- descriptor. Reg 7(1)(b): where two or more are each satisfied on over 50%, the one which scores the
-- higher or highest number of points. The two limbs are one selection over the candidates satisfied on
-- over 50% of the days: one candidate is limb (a), several are limb (b).
GIVEN es IS A LIST OF `a descriptor with the days on which it is satisfied`
      `the days of the required period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF `a descriptor with the days on which it is satisfied`
`reg 7(1)(a) and (b): the candidates satisfied on over 50% of the days` es `of` `the days of the required period` MEANS
    filter (GIVEN e YIELD `reg 7(1): this descriptor is satisfied on over 50% of the days of the required period` e `of` `the days of the required period`) es

-- src:69 | (a) where one descriptor is satisfied on over 50% of the days of the required period, that descriptor;
@ref reg 7(1)(a) (src:69)
GIVEN es IS A LIST OF `a descriptor with the days on which it is satisfied`
      `the days of the required period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `a row of Schedule 1`
`reg 7(1)(a): the descriptor satisfied on over 50% of the days, where one is` es `of` `the days of the required period` MEANS
    CONSIDER `reg 7(1)(a) and (b): the candidates satisfied on over 50% of the days` es `of` `the days of the required period`
    WHEN e FOLLOWED BY EMPTY THEN JUST (e's `the descriptor`)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:70 | (b) where two or more descriptors are each satisfied on over 50% of the days of the required period, the descriptor which scores the higher or highest number of points; and
@ref reg 7(1)(b) (src:70)
GIVEN es IS A LIST OF `a descriptor with the days on which it is satisfied`
      `the days of the required period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `a row of Schedule 1`
`reg 7(1)(b): the descriptor scoring the highest points, where two or more are each satisfied on over 50% of the days` es `of` `the days of the required period` MEANS
    IF count (`reg 7(1)(a) and (b): the candidates satisfied on over 50% of the days` es `of` `the days of the required period`) AT LEAST 2
    THEN CONSIDER `reg 7(1): the candidate scoring the highest number of points among` (`reg 7(1)(a) and (b): the candidates satisfied on over 50% of the days` es `of` `the days of the required period`)
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
         WHEN JUST e THEN JUST (e's `the descriptor`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- reg 7(1)(c): where no descriptor is satisfied on over 50% of the days but two or more descriptors
-- (other than a descriptor which scores 0 points) are satisfied for periods which, when added together,
-- amount to over 50% of the days: (i) the descriptor satisfied for the greater or greatest proportion of
-- days; or (ii) where both or all are satisfied for the same proportion, the one that scores the higher or
-- highest number of points. The descriptors added together, and chosen among, are those other than a
-- 0-point descriptor that are satisfied on at least one day (fork F-6).
GIVEN es IS A LIST OF `a descriptor with the days on which it is satisfied`
GIVETH A LIST OF `a descriptor with the days on which it is satisfied`
`reg 7(1)(c): the candidates other than a 0-point descriptor, satisfied on at least one day` es MEANS
    filter (GIVEN e YIELD    ((e's `the descriptor`)'s `its points` GREATER THAN 0)
                          AND (e's `the days of the required period on which it is satisfied`) GREATER THAN 0) es

-- src:71 | (c) where no descriptor is satisfied on over 50% of the days of the required period but two or more descriptors (other than a descriptor which scores 0 points) are satisfied for periods which, when added together, amount to over 50% of the days of the required period–
-- src:72 | (i) the descriptor which is satisfied for the greater or greatest proportion of days of the required period; or,
-- src:73 | (ii) where both or all descriptors are satisfied for the same proportion, the descriptor which scores the higher or highest number of points.
@ref reg 7(1)(c) (src:71-73)
GIVEN es IS A LIST OF `a descriptor with the days on which it is satisfied`
      `the days of the required period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 7(1)(c): no descriptor is satisfied on over 50% but two or more together are` es `of` `the days of the required period` MEANS
        null (`reg 7(1)(a) and (b): the candidates satisfied on over 50% of the days` es `of` `the days of the required period`)
    AND count (`reg 7(1)(c): the candidates other than a 0-point descriptor, satisfied on at least one day` es) AT LEAST 2
    AND (sum (map (GIVEN e YIELD e's `the days of the required period on which it is satisfied`) (`reg 7(1)(c): the candidates other than a 0-point descriptor, satisfied on at least one day` es))) TIMES 2
            GREATER THAN `the days of the required period`

@ref reg 7(1)(c)(i), reg 7(1)(c)(ii) (src:72-73)
GIVEN es IS A LIST OF `a descriptor with the days on which it is satisfied`
      `the days of the required period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `a row of Schedule 1`
`reg 7(1)(c): the descriptor that applies where none is satisfied on over 50% but two or more together are` es `of` `the days of the required period` MEANS
    IF `reg 7(1)(c): no descriptor is satisfied on over 50% but two or more together are` es `of` `the days of the required period`
    THEN CONSIDER `reg 7(1)(c): the candidate satisfied on the most days, then scoring the highest number of points, among` (`reg 7(1)(c): the candidates other than a 0-point descriptor, satisfied on at least one day` es)
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
         WHEN JUST e THEN JUST (e's `the descriptor`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- reg 7(1): the descriptor which applies to C in relation to each activity is, in the order of the
-- limbs: (a), then (b), then (c). The limbs are exclusive by their own conditions, so the order does
-- not change which applies. Where none of them selects a descriptor, the text does not say which
-- applies: NOTHING (fork F-7).
-- src:68 | (1) The descriptor which applies to C in relation to each activity in the tables referred to in regulations 5 and 6 is—
-- src:69 | (a) where one descriptor is satisfied on over 50% of the days of the required period, that descriptor;
-- src:70 | (b) where two or more descriptors are each satisfied on over 50% of the days of the required period, the descriptor which scores the higher or highest number of points; and
-- src:71 | (c) where no descriptor is satisfied on over 50% of the days of the required period but two or more descriptors (other than a descriptor which scores 0 points) are satisfied for periods which, when added together, amount to over 50% of the days of the required period–
-- src:72 | (i) the descriptor which is satisfied for the greater or greatest proportion of days of the required period; or,
-- src:73 | (ii) where both or all descriptors are satisfied for the same proportion, the descriptor which scores the higher or highest number of points.
@ref reg 7(1) (src:68-73)
GIVEN es IS A LIST OF `a descriptor with the days on which it is satisfied`
      `the days of the required period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `a row of Schedule 1`
`reg 7(1): the descriptor which applies to C in relation to the activity` es `of` `the days of the required period` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF isJust (`reg 7(1)(a): the descriptor satisfied on over 50% of the days, where one is` es `of` `the days of the required period`)
        THEN `reg 7(1)(a): the descriptor satisfied on over 50% of the days, where one is` es `of` `the days of the required period`
        IF isJust (`reg 7(1)(b): the descriptor scoring the highest points, where two or more are each satisfied on over 50% of the days` es `of` `the days of the required period`)
        THEN `reg 7(1)(b): the descriptor scoring the highest points, where two or more are each satisfied on over 50% of the days` es `of` `the days of the required period`
        OTHERWISE `reg 7(1)(c): the descriptor that applies where none is satisfied on over 50% but two or more together are` es `of` `the days of the required period`

§ `Regulations 8 to 11: information, consultation, good reason and fresh determination`

-- reg 8(1): the Secretary of State may require C to provide any information or evidence required to
-- determine whether C has limited or severely limited ability. A power of the Secretary of State and a
-- liability of C (Hohfeld); the question for C is what must be done in answer to it, below.
-- src:83 | (1) The Secretary of State may require C to provide any information or evidence required to determine whether C has limited ability or severely limited ability to carry out daily living activities or mobility activities.
@ref reg 8(1) (src:83)
GIVEN `the information or evidence is required to determine whether C has limited ability or severely limited ability` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 8(1): the Secretary of State may require C to provide the information or evidence` MEANS
    `the information or evidence is required to determine whether C has limited ability or severely limited ability`

-- reg 8(2): C must provide the information or evidence within one month from the date of the request, or
-- within such longer period as the Secretary of State may consider reasonable in the circumstances of the
-- particular case. The longer period is the Secretary of State's judgment and is the input (a date).
-- src:84 | (2) Where information or evidence is requested under paragraph (1), C must provide the information or evidence to the Secretary of State within one month from the date of the request being made or within such longer period as the Secretary of State may consider reasonable in the circumstances of the particular case.
@ref reg 8(2) (src:84)
GIVEN `the date of the request` IS A DATE
      `the later last day, if the Secretary of State considers a longer period reasonable` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 8(2): the last day for providing the information or evidence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the later last day, if the Secretary of State considers a longer period reasonable`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `add months` `the date of the request` 1
    WHEN JUST later THEN
        IF later AT LEAST (`add months` `the date of the request` 1)
        THEN later
        ELSE `add months` `the date of the request` 1

GIVEN `the last day for providing the information or evidence` IS A DATE
      `the day C provided it, if C has` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 8(2): C provided the information or evidence in time` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day C provided it, if C has`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST d THEN d AT MOST `the last day for providing the information or evidence`

-- reg 8(3): where C fails without good reason to comply with the request, a negative determination in
-- relation to the component to which the failure related must be made. Whether C had good reason is the
-- Secretary of State's judgment (informed by regulation 10) and is the input.
-- src:85 | (3) Where C fails without good reason to comply with the request referred to in paragraph (1), a negative determination in relation to the component to which the failure related must be made.
@ref reg 8(3) (src:85)
GIVEN `C provided the information or evidence in time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State is satisfied that C had good reason for not doing so` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 8(3): a negative determination must be made in relation to the component to which the failure related` MEANS
        (NOT `C provided the information or evidence in time`)
    AND (NOT `the Secretary of State is satisfied that C had good reason for not doing so`)

-- reg 9(1): where it falls to be determined whether C has limited or severely limited ability, C may be
-- required to attend for and participate in a consultation in person, or to participate by telephone or by
-- video, or both.
-- src:87 | (1) Where it falls to be determined whether C has limited ability or severely limited ability to carry out daily living activities or mobility activities, C may be required to do either or both of the following —
-- src:88 | (a) attend for and participate in a consultation in person;
-- src:89 | (b) participate in a consultation by telephone or by video or by video.
@ref reg 9(1) (src:87-89)
GIVEN `it falls to be determined whether C has limited ability or severely limited ability` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 9(1): C may be required to take part in a consultation` MEANS
    `it falls to be determined whether C has limited ability or severely limited ability`

-- reg 9(3) and (4): reg 9(2) does not apply unless (a) written notice of the date, time and, where
-- applicable, place of the consultation is sent to C at least 7 days in advance; or (b) C agrees, in writing or
-- otherwise, to accept a shorter period of notice. Written notice includes notice sent by electronic
-- communication where C has agreed to accept correspondence in that way.
-- src:91 | (3) Paragraph (2) does not apply unless —
-- src:92 | (a) written notice of the date, time and, where applicable, place for, the consultation is sent to C at least 7 days in advance; or
-- src:93 | (b) C agrees, whether in writing or otherwise, to accept a shorter period of notice of those matters.
-- src:94 | (4) In paragraph (3), reference to written notice includes notice sent by electronic communication where C has agreed to accept correspondence in that way and ‘electronic communication’ has the meaning given in section 15(1) of the Electronic Communications Act 2000 .
@ref reg 9(3), reg 9(4) (src:91-94)
GIVEN `the day the notice was sent` IS A DATE
      `the day of the consultation` IS A DATE
      `the notice was in writing on paper` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice was sent by electronic communication` IS A BOOLEAN
      `C had agreed to accept correspondence by electronic communication` IS A BOOLEAN
      `C agreed to accept a shorter period of notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 9(3): regulation 9(2) can apply because the notice requirement is met` MEANS
        (   (   `the notice was in writing on paper`
             OR (   `the notice was sent by electronic communication`
                 AND `C had agreed to accept correspondence by electronic communication`))
         AND (Day `the day of the consultation` MINUS Day `the day the notice was sent`) AT LEAST 7)
     OR `C agreed to accept a shorter period of notice`

-- reg 9(2), with reg 9(5): subject to paragraph (3), where C fails without good reason to attend for or
-- participate in a consultation, a negative determination must be made. "Consultation" is a consultation
-- with a person approved by the Secretary of State (reg 9(5)). Good reason is the Secretary of State's
-- judgment (informed by regulation 10) and is the input.
-- src:90 | (2) Subject to paragraph (3), where C fails without good reason to attend for or participate in a consultation referred to in paragraph (1), a negative determination must be made.
-- src:95 | (5) In this regulation, a reference to consultation is to a consultation with a person approved by the Secretary of State.
@ref reg 9(2), reg 9(5) (src:90, src:95)
GIVEN `the consultation is with a person approved by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `C failed to attend for or participate in the consultation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State is satisfied that C had good reason for the failure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice requirement of regulation 9(3) is met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 9(2): a negative determination must be made because C failed to attend or participate` MEANS
        `the consultation is with a person approved by the Secretary of State`
    AND `C failed to attend for or participate in the consultation`
    AND (NOT `the Secretary of State is satisfied that C had good reason for the failure`)
    AND `the notice requirement of regulation 9(3) is met`

-- reg 10: the matters to be taken into account in determining whether C has good reason under reg 8(3) or
-- 9(2) include (a) C's state of health at the relevant time; and (b) the nature of any disability that C has.
-- "Include" makes the list a floor: the rule says which matters the regulation requires to be taken into
-- account; for any other matter it is silent, so the answer FALSE means "regulation 10 does not itself require it".
DECLARE `a matter that may bear on good reason` IS ONE OF
    `C's state of health at the relevant time`
    `the nature of any disability that C has`
    `any other matter`

-- src:97 | The matters to be taken into account in determining whether C has good reason under regulation 8(3) or 9(2) include —
-- src:98 | (a) C's state of health at the relevant time; and
-- src:99 | (b) the nature of any disability that C has.
@ref reg 10 (src:97-99)
GIVEN m IS A `a matter that may bear on good reason`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 10: regulation 10 requires this matter to be taken into account in determining good reason` m MEANS
       m EQUALS `C's state of health at the relevant time`
    OR m EQUALS `the nature of any disability that C has`

-- reg 11(1): where it has been determined that C has limited or severely limited ability, the Secretary of
-- State may, for any reason and at any time, determine afresh in accordance with reg 4 whether C
-- continues to have it. Reg 11(2): doing work for payment or in expectation of payment, or doing voluntary
-- work, is not a reason for a fresh determination.
DECLARE `a reason for determining afresh` IS ONE OF
    `C is doing work for payment or in expectation of payment`
    `C is doing voluntary work`
    `any other reason`

-- src:101 | (1) Subject to paragraph (2), where it has been determined that C has limited ability or severely limited ability to carry out either or both daily living activities or mobility activities, the Secretary of State may, for any reason and at any time, determine afresh in accordance with regulation 4 whether C continues to have such limited ability or severely limited ability.
-- src:102 | (2) For the purposes of paragraph (1), doing work for payment or in expectation of payment, or doing voluntary work, is not a reason for a fresh determination.
@ref reg 11(1), reg 11(2) (src:101-102)
GIVEN `it has been determined that C has limited ability or severely limited ability` IS A BOOLEAN
      reason IS A `a reason for determining afresh`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 11: the Secretary of State may determine afresh whether C continues to have limited or severely limited ability, for this reason` MEANS
        `it has been determined that C has limited ability or severely limited ability`
    AND (NOT (   reason EQUALS `C is doing work for payment or in expectation of payment`
              OR reason EQUALS `C is doing voluntary work`))
